This project is an independent implementation. It is inspired by, and owes its
approach to, two earlier projects:

  * jaychang1989/dsh-webchat (Apache-2.0), Copyright 2026 jaychang1989 —
    https://github.com/jaychang1989/dsh-webchat
  * xmuwenxiang/dsh-web-chat (Apache-2.0), the predecessor of the above —
    https://github.com/xmuwenxiang/dsh-web-chat

Reused from those projects (concepts and platform integration patterns, no
source files copied):

  * the dual-face packaging of a DSH plugin — a Host half exported as ".", a
    browser half exported as "./client" and declared through `dsh.client`, and a
    `cordis.patch.yml` bundle row;
  * the `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })` form of the emitted
    client bundle and the `{ inject: ['slots'], apply }` module shape;
  * rendering the official site through the desktop shell's native browser guest
    (`dshDesktop.browser.acquire` + `<webview>`), keeping the guest outside the
    React tree so hiding the panel never tears it down;
  * carrying the page's own `localStorage` and `document.cookie` across restarts,
    and the user-agent treatment that removes the `Electron/<version>` token.

Written for this project:

  * the persistence design and its guard rails: no `electron` import, a snapshot
    that a logged-out page cannot degrade, an explicit logout path, and
    diagnostics that never expose credential values;
  * the Host routes (state/index.js), the client flow, the tests and this
    documentation;
  * the decision to drop the window fallbacks (BrowserWindow, chromeless
    Edge/Chrome, system browser), which cannot work in the Desktop Host and are
    out of scope for a Desktop-only panel.

No file from either project was copied into this repository. Behaviour that
looks identical is the platform's contract, not a shared implementation.
